{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541537-beast-pandora-s-box","id":541537,"title":"Beast: Pandora's Box","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-05T12:04:03-07:00","id":541537,"title":"Beast: Pandora's Box","content":"&quot;So you think you know the Dark Mother? Do you ever wonder why we are trapped within this damned narrative of fighting heroes for...what exactly?<br /> <br /> Back when human's we're stumbling around, being hunted and hounded, Something lay deep within the astral. Something hungry. When all of these human ideas and creations appeared within the layers of the astral plane, this Chthonian being would feed on human's passion, their creativity, their love. <br /> <br /> No one knows where she came from, but they say The Dark Mother sought to starve this creature. To protect what she could. <br /> <br /> Due to the frail nature of the world back then, humans saw terrible things, and those ideas, those symbols of fear, were the most abundant in the Temenos. She took the 'monsters' humans dreamed of and wrapped them around what she tried to protect most. Human 'hope'.<br /> <br /> Thus, wanting to or not, The first beast soul was made, and slowly, The real monster, the one the Dark Mother wished to starve, fell asleep.<br /> <br /> I know. it's hard to believe that we, the monsters of man, are the reason for human's drive to learn and live, but it is true. we are now an essential part of the world. Yes we must sate our hunger in order to stay strong, and it may be wrong, or harmful, but we do it to keep our souls strong. To keep the hope alive.<br /> <br /> Every Beast soul is a pandora's box.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Now heroes..They are sad stories within themselves. People who have lost everything, who are willing to do what they must to survive. Of course it's understandable to seek out a reason for their problems. and we believe that what they see are 'monsters who have made their lives a living hell', <br /> <br /> but that's not what they see. <br /> <br /> They see us, and they see the hope that lies within the heart of our lairs. They see the promise that if they can claim it for themselves, they can be better, they can have an end to justify the means.<br /> <br /> which is beautiful, but I don't plan on dying for them to realize it was never our fault to begin&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I hope the next time you see a hero, you will understand them a little more.<br /> I hope the next time you hunt, you will understand that you must to feed your soul, to keep hope alive.<br /> <br /> It's hard having to kill, and to terrorize, but we do it to continue The Dark Mother's act of keeping the True Monster asleep.<br /> Let us be the monsters, so they don't see what a monster really is.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T12:28:33-07:00","id":541567,"title":"","content":"This is a neat idea. The concept of tying Pandora's Box to the Dark Mother alone is compelling.<br /> <br /> Also, it reminds me of the most recent season finale of <i>Supernatural</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:38:31-07:00","id":541645,"title":"","content":"The idea that the Dark Mother may be the other side of the Chaoskampf is actually genius!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:51:06-07:00","id":541965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541537-beast-pandora-s-box?p=541567#post541567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The concept of tying Pandora's Box to the Dark Mother alone is compelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth pointing out that it's nigh-textual in the core \u2014 check the Anakim writeup again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T23:24:18-07:00","id":542324,"title":"","content":"I don't quite understand what Pandora's Box has to do with everything else you wrote, but I do find that all to be a very compelling mythology for the game. Maybe elaborate on why Beasts must feed: why are the monsters motivated to feed off of humans in various ways? How does this help starve the True Monster? By destroying the passion, creativity, and love that feeds it? What is it that humans are hoping for that must be protected? Why is the lair connected to hope? I like the general ideas you've got, but it seems a bit jumbled and unclear to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5697-n_a_anyon","name":"n_a_anyon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T04:21:56-07:00","id":542437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts must feed: why are the monsters motivated to feed off of humans in various ways? </div> </div> </div>Because they are astral entities. Astral entities are made of thought, and represent concepts and ideas experienced by people in the physical world. Beasts represent Fear, and thus they sustain themselves by creating that fear in various ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>n_a_anyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541537-beast-pandora-s-box?p=542324#post542324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't quite understand what Pandora's Box has to do with everything else you wrote, but I do find that all to be a very compelling mythology for the game. Maybe elaborate on why Beasts must feed: why are the monsters motivated to feed off of humans in various ways? How does this help starve the True Monster? By destroying the passion, creativity, and love that feeds it? What is it that humans are hoping for that must be protected? Why is the lair connected to hope? I like the general ideas you've got, but it seems a bit jumbled and unclear to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the OP's story, an alien astral entity, which feeds on passion and creativity, threatens to overwhelm all other astral concepts. The Dark Mother, in an attempt to protect other astral entities from this invader, looks to the second-strongest astral entities - human fears. By combining strong human fears with the weak concept of hope, she creates a new entity, Beasts, which feed on the same things as the invader. Because while fears torment mankind, the hope that those fears may be overcome drives and inspires us to do great deeds. With mankind's passion and creativity focused towards overcoming its fears, beasts prospered, and the passion and creativity which used to feed the invader began to fade.<br /> <br /> Heroes are fundamentally hopeless people. They've lost everything. When they see a Beast, they see not only the things that have been holding them back all this time, but also the hope that by overcoming that beast, they can rise out of their abysmal situation. Because that is, fundamentally, what Beasts represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-06-2015, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:30:50-07:00","id":542580,"title":"","content":"Maybe I missed something here, but I fail to see how the starved monster is an actual monster.<br /> <br /> If Beasts feed on terror and they spread terror in order to satiate themselves, then logically speaking the monster who feeds on positive emotions and ideas would spread them in order to satiate itself. And if creatures of the Astral World are products of thought, then encouraging human creativity would actually spawn more of these things; not less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-06-2015, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:21:58-07:00","id":543289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541537-beast-pandora-s-box?p=542580#post542580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I missed something here, but I fail to see how the starved monster is an actual monster.<br /> <br /> If Beasts feed on terror and they spread terror in order to satiate themselves, then logically speaking the monster who feeds on positive emotions and ideas would spread them in order to satiate itself. And if creatures of the Astral World are products of thought, then encouraging human creativity would actually spawn more of these things; not less.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it were a typical astral entity, yes it would spread those ideas. However, we're left to assume that this creature is atypical, and an abberation among astral entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}